course: dictionary
lesson: 11166
title: Windscreen or windshield?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A windscreen is the large glass window at the front of a car, bus or other vehicle. To work out a new word, read the words around it. «Some cars have a rain sensor that shines invisible light at the windscreen and switches the wipers on when raindrops change the reflection.» Rain hits the glass and the wipers clear it, so the windscreen must be the glass at the front.
explain: «Park a car under a lime tree in July and come back to a windscreen covered in sticky drops.» The sticky drops are on the glass at the front of the car. Check by swapping in your meaning: "come back to a front window covered in sticky drops" still makes sense, so you have got it right.
explain: Windscreen is the word used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. In the USA and Canada people say windshield for the same thing. If you read windshield in a book from America, you can use the meaning you already know.
fact: A windscreen is the large glass window at the front of a car, bus or other vehicle.
fact: Windscreen wipers clear rain from the windscreen.
fact: Before you drive, you clear the windscreen of ice.
fact: In the USA and Canada, the same thing is called a windshield.
fact: Windscreens are made of special safety glass.
exercise: «Park a car under a lime tree in July and come back to a windscreen covered in sticky drops.» What is a windscreen? | *The large glass window at the front of a car | A metal door at the back of a bus | A tyre that grips the road | A small mirror inside the car
exercise: It is pouring with rain, so Dad switches on the windscreen wipers. What do the wipers clear? | Dust from the seats | *Rain from the windscreen | Crumbs from the floor | Leaves from the roof
exercise: An American book says, «The windshield was cracked.» What does windshield mean? | A fine for parking | A kind of hat for drivers | *The same as a windscreen, the glass at the front of a car | A window at the back of a bus
test: Which country says windscreen rather than windshield? | Canada | Mexico | United States | *Australia
test: «A yellow plastic packet stuck to the windscreen is a parking ticket.» What is the yellow packet? | A sticker for a bus | *A parking ticket | A map of the town | A flower
exam: «Crashes with moose are dangerous because long legs put the heavy body at windscreen height.» Where is the moose body in that sentence? | Under the road | At the top of the trees | Lying in a field | *At the height of the glass at the front of a car
